      "code": "rt_buffer_t buffer = { .bytes = (char *)Data, .size = Size, .used = Size };",
      "note": "The entire attacker-controlled byte string is wrapped, without any copy or validation, into an rt_buffer_t whose bytes/used fields back every subsequent io->read call. Both the tainted n_missing_values field and the 0x20 bytes that ultimately corrupt info->label come from this buffer.",
      "kind": "source"
