      "file": "src/spss/readstat_spss.c",
      "function": "spss_varinfo_free",
      "line": null,
      "code": "free(info->label);",
      "note": "free() is called on info->label, which the heap overflow has replaced with the non-heap value 0x202020. This pointer was never returned by an allocator, so ASan's Deallocate reads the would-be chunk header 16 bytes below it, at 0x202010, and takes a SEGV on that unmapped address. 0x202010 is exactly the fault address reported in the staged sanitizer trace, which pins info->label == 0x202020 at the sink.",
